ents (like aces, double faults, or long rallies) visible in the provided frames for the first game. The frames primarily show the setup for the first point and the scoreboard indicating Serena has won the first point.\n\n4.  **The final outcome of the first game (who wins):**\n    The final outcome of the first game is not shown in the provided frames. The frames only capture the beginning of the first game, with Serena having won the first point (15-0). The game is still in progress at the end of the provided sequence.\n\n5.  **Scoreboard information showing the 1-0 lead:**\n    The scoreboard information in Frame 7 and Frame 8 shows the score as "V. WILLIAMS 0" and "S. WILLIAMS 1". This indicates that Serena Williams has won one point in the game (15-0), not that she has won the game (which would be 1-0 in games). The "1" on Serena\'s side represents 15 points, not 1 game. Therefore, the scoreboard does not show a 1-0 lead in games; it shows a 15-0 lead in points for Serena Williams in the first game.\n\nIn summary, the provided frames show the very beginning of the match, with Serena Williams serving first and winning the first point of the first game (15-0). The outcome of the first game and any subsequent points are not visible in the given frames.'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0001.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0005.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0010.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0015.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0020.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0025.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0030.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame_0035.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/tKIFQI9cH2c/frames/frame